ed as an egress policy on eth2 (facing node3), capping all node2→node3 traffic to 1 Mbit/s while eth1 (facing node2) stays unshaped for the reverse direction. Verified with iperf3: node2→node3 settled at ~1.04 Mbit/s, node3→node2 reached ~1.5+ Gbit/s unrestricted. All four nodes were restarted one at a time with boot_id changes proving real reboots, and all state (static IPs, routes, VyOS shaper config) was confirmed to persist. Caught and fixed a reconciler gotcha: an ad-hoc SSH key drop into VyOS's authorized_keys file was wiped on reboot by VyOS's login reconciler; replaced with a proper `set system login user vyos authentication public-keys` config entry which persisted, and re-ran the playbook to confirm idempotency and full recovery.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed topology via environment.toml: node1=VyOS router with eth0(mgmt)/eth1(lan-a)/eth2(lan-b), node2=AlmaLinux eth0(mgmt)/eth1(lan-a), node3=AlmaLinux eth0(mgmt)/eth1(lan-b), node4=Ubuntu control node with ansible-core installed\",\"Set up passwordless cluster SSH (cluster_ed25519 key) from node4 to root@node2, root@node3, and vyos@node1 with passwordless sudo to root\",\"Diagnosed VyOS quirk: the configure/commit/save alias-based CLI session only initializes correctly when the script runs as root (sudo), not as the vyos user directly - fixed by using ansible_become=sudo on the vyos host\",\"Built /root/ansible/{ansible.cfg,inventory.ini,site.yml} on node4 defining lan_endpoints (node2,node3) and vyos_router (node1) groups\",\"Playbook: configured static IPv4 on node2/node3's eth1 via community.general.nmcli plus a route to the peer's LAN subnet via node1's gateway IP; installed iperf3 for testing\",\"Playbook: pushed VyOS config on node1 setting eth1=10.10.10.1/24, eth2=10.10.20.1/24, and a qos policy shaper LIMIT-TO-NODE3 (bandwidth 1mbit, default class 100%) applied as egress policy on eth2 only\",\"Ran the playbook successfully (idempotent on re-run), verified interface addresses, routes, and tc qdisc (htb on eth2, plain fq_codel on eth1)\",\"Verified traffic shaping empirically with iperf3: node2->node3 throughput capped near 1 Mbit/s; node3->node2 throughput unrestricted (~1.5+ Gbit/s); opened/closed firewalld port 5201 on node2/node3 for the test only\",\"Executed mandatory restart protocol on all 4 nodes sequentially (node1, node2, node3, node4): captured boot_id + health baseline, issued a deferred `reboot`, polled until exec succeeded again, confirmed changed boot_id, and verified recovered state (IPs, routes, VyOS shaper config) after each restart\",\"After node1's reboot, the re-run playbook failed because the manually-appended SSH key in /home/vyos/.ssh/authorized_keys had been regenerated by VyOS's login reconciler; fixed by adding the key through `set system login user vyos authentication public-keys` in VyOS config (persists across reboots) and re-verified idempotent playbook run\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 reach each other only through node1 (separate private networks, static addressing since dhcp=false)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1b6e8d65158a4081\",\"cmd-aa1e7895a6514017\",\"cmd-21ef2b6292234a6f\",\"cmd-6216f21241584368\"],\"summary\":\"Ansible playbook run shows changed=3 on node2/node3 applying static IPs (10.10.10.2/24, 10.10.20.2/24) and cross-subnet routes via node1; post-run `ip addr`/`ip route` on both nodes confirm the addresses and routes via 10.10.10.1/10.10.20.1\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 (VyOS) configured as router with static IPs on eth1/eth2, implemented via Ansible\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-aa1e7895a6514017\",\"cmd-856d7ad7e5d342b5\"],\"summary\":\"Playbook task 'Push VyOS configuration' returned changed:[node1]; config.boot on node1 shows eth1=10.10.10.1/24 and eth2=10.10.20.1/24 persisted\"},{\"requirement\":\"Traffic from node2 toward node3 limited to 1 Mbit/s\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-46333873aadb4d5f\",\"cmd-5c1b7c0b630f468f\"],\"summary\":\"tc qdisc show on node1 eth2 shows htb root qdisc from the qos 